    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Symbotic Inc. describes itself as a provider of end-to-end warehouse automation solutions for retailers and distributors. Its site says the company's systems combine robotics with AI-enhanced software to increase facility capacity through dense storage, maximize throughput, and create efficiency gains across the supply chain. The company states its solutions can handle palletized goods, small quantity fulfillment, and omnichannel operations, with goods as small as 1 lb (0.5 kg) and 2 x 6.4 x 5 in (5.1 x 16.3 x 12.7 cm) to as large as 60 lb (27.2 kg) and 36 x 24 x 16.2 in (91.4 x 61 x 41.2 cm), including cold chain requirements.\n\nOn AI, the site presents AI-enhanced software as a core part of its systems, saying the software \"sees beyond your warehouse walls\" and expands operational possibilities. No specific AI product names are given in the material. The company describes itself as a leader in industrial automation and technology at large, with a purpose of getting the right goods to people who need them.\n\nSymbotic Inc. is a public, for-profit company headquartered in Wilmington, Massachusetts, trading under ticker SYM with CIK 0001837240. It is also listed under the aliases Symbotic Inc. and SYMBOTIC INC. The company is associated with 191 Massachusetts law exposure matters. No litigation cases are recorded for the company.",
